    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1ec36a5e83d06983e1dbfec1262daa2f5f94107e86674ea1875129fd3a3b1111",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The cyclicity upgrade survives the passage from the continuous Hardy/L2 setting to the reciprocal-interval discretization. In the Hardy realization, multiplicative inner-function isometries propagate E to Mellin images of a total family of initial-interval indicators; in M, integer dilation isometries propagate 1 to the corresponding discrete total family. Together the units show that one-vector closure implies totality by the same invariant-subspace mechanism before and after discretization, rather than by a new approximation argument.",
