    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_9cae327c21726f9d542aa2e13c18d910348571c299ef6f27d59f010f9ade659e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source identifies one approximation problem in linked coordinates: the Mellin isometry sends the constant function and fractional-part generators to E and the Hardy generators, while restriction to the reciprocal-interval subspace selects the discrete family and the sampling unitary sends that family and its constant target to the weighted sequences. Thus the continuous L2, Hardy, piecewise-constant, and weighted-sequence closure criteria are connected by explicit target-and-generator maps rather than merely sharing RH as a conclusion.",
