    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c6ca1a9e7b09c6d49dd2b48ddd1ab20fab1dc4ed394caad3bfa72e1c25862723",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The two directions of the Hardy-space RH criterion use complementary mechanisms. Under RH, regularized finite Mobius combinations of the discrete generators converge in two controlled stages to E; if RH fails, evaluation at one interior zeta zero is a continuous functional that annihilates every generator but not E. The coefficient support in the forward construction further shows that square-free-index generators suffice for this one-vector closure criterion.",
